        "date_posted": "",
        "is_remote": false,
        "description": "WriftAI is building the infrastructure layer that makes AI easy to deploy and scale in production. We help teams ship AI\\-powered products faster by removing the operational complexity behind running models at scale — enabling customers to focus on building, not infrastructure. Our platform provides simple APIs and SDKs that handle model deployment, scaling, and performance optimization behind the scenes, making production\\-grade AI accessible to engineering teams of all sizes.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n We're looking for fresh graduates in Computer Science or Engineering who are eager to start their careers as Software Engineers and drive the future of AI.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**The Role** \n\n\n\n\n We’re looking for a\n **Software Development Engineer** \n to help build and evolve the core systems that power the WriftAI platform. This role focuses on developing product\\-facing services, APIs, and internal systems that enable developers to deploy, manage, and scale AI workloads reliably.\n \n\n\n\n You’ll work closely with Platform Engineers, Product, and other engineers to deliver features that are robust, scalable, and easy to use.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**What You'll Do** \n\n\n\n* Design and build backend services and APIs that power WriftAI’s core platform.\n* Build and evolve systems that integrate directly with AI model inference, configuration, and lifecycle management.\n* Implement features that improve reliability, performance, and usability for developers.\n* Work hands\\-on with AI\\-powered features, experimenting with model behavior, performance characteristics, and developer\\-facing interfaces.\n* Collaborate with Platform Engineers to integrate application logic with underlying infrastructure.\n* Contribute to system design and architecture discussions.\n* Debug and resolve issues across services in production environments.\n* Write clear, maintainable, and well\\-tested code.\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**What We Need From You** \n\n\n\n* Graduated less than 24 months ago or about to complete a Bachelor’s or Master’s Degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, or related fields at time of application\n* Proficiency in at least one backend programming language (e.g., Go, Python, Java, or similar).\n* Experience in deploying machine learning models in a cloud environment.\n* Strong analytical and problem\\-solving skills, with a flair for creative solutions.\n* Knowledge of Computer Science fundamentals such as object\\-oriented design, algorithm design, data structures, problem solving and complexity analysis.\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Nice to have** \n\n\n\n* Experience working hands\\-on with AI\\-powered systems, such as integrating model inference, experimenting with prompts or configurations, or building features on top of AI models.\n* Familiarity with cloud\\-based systems or distributed architectures.\n* Experience building or supporting high\\-throughput systems, data pipelines, or AI\\-powered products.\n* Familiarity with observability tools and production debugging workflows.\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Why WriftAI?** \n\n\n\n* **Solve Real AI Challenges** \n : Work on infrastructure that removes the operational complexity of deploying and scaling AI in production.\n* **Build with Innovation:** \n Be part of a team creating tooling that empowers developers to run AI workloads anywhere.\n* **High Impact** \n : Contribute meaningfully at an early but scaling company where individual ownership matters.\n* **Collaborative Culture** \n : Work alongside passionate engineers, product builders, and go\\-to\\-market professionals.\n* **Competitive Compensation** \n : Market\\-competitive compensation aligned with experience.\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n*WriftAI is proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees.*",
